#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073445 :question/id #uuid "e9aae52c-65f3-5dff-bc6b-a530f8c7acc1" :question/math-academy-id "e-13009" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y=4 \\\\ x+2y=16\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It doesn't matter which equation we pick first, so we choose the easiest one. In this case, the first equation looks like the easiest.\n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $x$ by adding $y$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y & =4 \\\\ x & =4+y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we replace $x$ with $4+y$ in the second equation and solve for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\tx+2y &=16 \\\n\t(4+y) + 2y &=16\\\n\t4+3y &=16\\\n\t3y &=12\\\n\ty &=4\n}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $y=4$ into $x=4+y$, then we can find the value of $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\tx &= 4 + y \\\n\t   &= 4 + (4) \\\n\t   &=8\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x = 8$ and $y = 4$, which can be written as $(8, 4).$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048678 :topic/math-academy-id 2225 :topic/title "Introduction to Systems of Linear Equations"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050622 :topic/math-academy-id 356 :topic/title "Solving Two-Variable Equations"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074030 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "c3a49164-4f9d-597a-9dc6-abf7860aa4ba" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070261} {:answer-field/id #uuid "795f6bc6-c4b4-5520-883c-77f20cec08ce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070262}] :question/id #uuid "acc0a44e-6eb6-5a95-a139-3841ec88693b" :question/math-academy-id "q-171690" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n${x + 5y = 13; y = x + 5$\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.The solution is\n$($\n{{field-1}}\n$$,\n{{field-2}}\n$)$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074172 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b643d8b6-388a-54ab-b235-3715b075ca10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071271} {:answer/id #uuid "b7ca0af2-c9e2-50b8-aa82-29c811387109" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071272} {:answer/id #uuid "db6b16f5-5009-56b0-8dbc-feec7e3509af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071273} {:answer/id #uuid "4284c760-b4f9-5590-8b60-e0effdb4b5dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071274} {:answer/id #uuid "4fbb9be1-44f2-5b9e-84d5-cc040bbae729" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071275}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4b7102cd-5458-52ab-8b4b-346cb2e5c0d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071270}] :question/id #uuid "963fb1bc-3f29-5c06-94a9-37168b40e1c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-4133" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n${3a + 2b = 4; - 4a + b = 2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "831b8a12-3240-5543-8f0b-63a066174430" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071349} {:answer/id #uuid "e71abec1-af90-564e-96cc-65f749dff99a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071350} {:answer/id #uuid "f9bd14c8-f201-5c70-ba77-5489006197a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071351} {:answer/id #uuid "30891c0a-e32e-5e99-9826-2629f5f5792b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071352} {:answer/id #uuid "424e6c76-ef65-55f4-bb2c-05129500785f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071353}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4ff0f62d-b46f-5fed-abea-e9c339cbff76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071348}] :question/id #uuid "5c71bd6b-b9a3-5587-89f4-a14a2c760bc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-5179" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $p - q$?\n\n${3p = 15; p + 2q = 9$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233560 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d447476e-6786-52c0-9a5b-aa6aa6b42f96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d447476e-6786-52c0-9a5b-aa6aa6b42f96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232246} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6f81397-282c-55bf-a574-31b7a7eb6872" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0d9ee9f-e333-5485-a7ba-ff333f3a6931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "600" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232248}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0d9ee9f-e333-5485-a7ba-ff333f3a6931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "600" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232248} :answer-field/id #uuid "e81a89a6-5e45-5c38-944f-815f8eebc873" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232247}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ba03c851-f080-5b98-bcba-fc2174ffc663" :question/math-academy-id "q-167194" :question/problem "The coefficients $a$ and $b$ also satisfy the equation $20b+400a=7\\,200.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$b\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}b=480-10a \\\\ 20b+400a=7\\,200\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the first equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=480-10a\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $b$ in the second equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20b+400a & =7\\,200 \\\\ 20(480-10a)+400a & =7\\,200 \\\\ 9\\,600-200a+400a & =7\\,200 \\\\ 9\\,600+200a & =7\\,200 \\\\ 200a & =-2\\,400 \\\\ a & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-12$ into $b=480-10a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =480-10(-12) \\\\ b & =600\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-12,\\,b=600.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233567 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25f6ebe2-11a4-50a4-afb6-e54166d6b757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25f6ebe2-11a4-50a4-afb6-e54166d6b757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232262} :answer-field/id #uuid "d89c06a2-d40d-59be-aba2-b51cfcb77eb2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232261} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81d5e96b-1699-54bb-87d3-abe3b34a48dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "320" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81d5e96b-1699-54bb-87d3-abe3b34a48dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "320" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232264} :answer-field/id #uuid "80788b1d-1ccd-5c42-ae32-41ab3f383746" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232263}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d104504e-e7b5-56df-8154-499bbc1d3f80" :question/math-academy-id "q-167210" :question/problem "The coefficients $a$ and $b$ also satisfy the equation $30b+900a=6\\,000.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$b\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}b=240-20a \\\\ 30b+900a=6\\,000\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the first equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=240-20a\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $b$ in the second equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}30b+900a & =6\\,000 \\\\ 30(240-20a)+900a & =6\\,000 \\\\ 7\\,200-600a+900a & =6\\,000 \\\\ 7\\,200+300a & =6\\,000 \\\\ 300a & =-1\\,200 \\\\ a & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-4$ into $b=240-20a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =240-20(-4) \\\\ b & =320\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-4,\\,b=320.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233574 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74b8ef99-22cc-5e49-9884-ae62824c5059" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74b8ef99-22cc-5e49-9884-ae62824c5059" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232278} :answer-field/id #uuid "194751b6-0ff6-5047-a6e8-f7e3cfbe1451" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232277} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39731897-add5-5068-a83a-649fb0aa6e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39731897-add5-5068-a83a-649fb0aa6e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232280} :answer-field/id #uuid "03a21b91-803e-51b3-8b0d-859c1f623d17" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232279}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6afc1799-60d6-5f69-94a5-994731079a93" :question/math-academy-id "q-167226" :question/problem "The coefficients $a$ and $b$ also satisfy the equation $70a+9b=600.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$b\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}b=75-5a \\\\ 70a+9b=600\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the first equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=75-5a\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $b$ in the second equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}70a+9b & =600 \\\\ 70a+9(75-5a) & =600 \\\\ 70a+675-45a & =600 \\\\ 25a+675 & =600 \\\\ 25a & =-75 \\\\ a & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-3$ into $b=75-5a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =75-5(-3) \\\\ b & =90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-3,\\,b=90.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496226 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51c5dada-d996-51cf-94d1-ca897ceda4c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51c5dada-d996-51cf-94d1-ca897ceda4c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495696} :answer-field/id #uuid "da300820-d65a-54b5-a122-648e1be4ca42" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496194} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0db68d80-560b-5294-a3e9-812966c11801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0db68d80-560b-5294-a3e9-812966c11801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495542} :answer-field/id #uuid "e16e42d5-5e57-5702-bb36-98fb0bad0dd6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496198}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "07b5302b-d797-5328-827e-aa28a460f929" :question/math-academy-id "q-181149" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4u-6v=-3 \\\\ u=-v-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(u,v)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(u,v)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It so happens that the second equation is already solved for $u:$\n\n$$\nu=-v-2\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $u$ with $-v-2$ in the first equation and solve for $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4u-6v & =-3 \\\\ 4(-v-2)-6v & =-3 \\\\ -4v-8-6v & =-3 \\\\ -10v & =5 \\\\ v & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $v=-\\frac{1}{2}$ into $u=-v-2,$ then we can find the value of $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =-v-2 \\\\ u & =-(-\\frac{1}{2})-2 \\\\ u & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=-\\frac{3}{2},\\,v=-\\frac{1}{2},$ which can be expressed as $(-\\frac{3}{2},-\\frac{1}{2}).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496255 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "001fa025-6178-5ba4-b287-f99d23255489" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "001fa025-6178-5ba4-b287-f99d23255489" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495509} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c44ea3f-ae01-5f06-b1d9-d8a1d677d43e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496138} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2cf528e-9238-53c7-ac72-2595f6c61117" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2cf528e-9238-53c7-ac72-2595f6c61117" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496013} :answer-field/id #uuid "d81fe473-caed-55d0-ae06-56890f9a6929" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496191}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4c3907fe-c83e-5bd5-ac54-297aa503451b" :question/math-academy-id "q-181175" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y=-4 \\\\ x-3y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(x,y)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It doesn't matter which equation we pick first, so we choose the easiest one. In this case, the second equation looks like the easiest.\n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $x$ by adding $3y$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\nx=3y-8\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $x$ with $3y-8$ in the first equation and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+y & =-4 \\\\ -2(3y-8)+y & =-4 \\\\ -6y+16+y & =-4 \\\\ -5y & =-20 \\\\ y & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $y=4$ into $x=3y-8,$ then we can find the value of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3y-8 \\\\ x & =3(4)-8 \\\\ x & =12-8 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=4,\\,y=4,$ which can be expressed as $(4,4).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497411 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "951ed025-e4b5-517b-830a-a3da54b9c6e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "951ed025-e4b5-517b-830a-a3da54b9c6e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496968} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c523c48-ec60-5fa0-9eec-5d07498f1571" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eebbe5cc-91ee-5b03-9257-cc5f956ce523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eebbe5cc-91ee-5b03-9257-cc5f956ce523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497171} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb7943f0-b18a-5a1c-9e1c-77a8a3b53234" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497319}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ededc7bf-b310-5714-a047-930df525362b" :question/math-academy-id "q-166843" :question/problem "The pastry shop's total cost and revenue per month (in dollars) from selling cakes can be modeled by the equations $y=1\\,600+5n$ and $y=64+17n,$ respectively, where $n$ is the number of cakes sold. \n\nSolve the system below using the substitution method to find the exact number of cakes needed to break even and the revenue made.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1\\,600+5n \\\\ y=64+17n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pastry shop breaks even when$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$cakes are produced. \n\nThe revenue made when selling this number of cakes is$\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,$dollars." :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that $y$ is isolated in the first equation. Therefore, we can replace $y$ with $1\\,600+5n$ in the second equation and solve for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =64+17n \\\\ 1\\,600+5n & =64+17n \\\\ 1\\,600+5n-64 & =64+17n-64 \\\\ 1\\,536+5n & =17n \\\\ 1\\,536+5n-5n & =17n-5n \\\\ 1\\,536 & =12n \\\\ \\frac{1\\,536}{12} & =\\frac{12n}{12} \\\\ 128 & =n \\\\ n & =128\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $n=128$ into $y=64+17n$, then we can find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=64+17(128)=2\\,240\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the solution to the system of equations is $n=128$ and $y=2\\,240.$\nTherefore, the pastry shop breaks even when $128$ units are produced, and the revenue made when selling this number of units is $$2\\,240.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503753 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e2466bb-be73-57a5-a448-e2ae0ba60c2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e2466bb-be73-57a5-a448-e2ae0ba60c2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503039} :answer-field/id #uuid "163d9f6a-4519-5200-83a3-6d401cb44c91" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503523} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13a5bcc9-bf29-57f7-9c4f-15fe366965e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "540" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13a5bcc9-bf29-57f7-9c4f-15fe366965e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "540" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503022} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d99e451-ff6c-54c5-be9e-d8c096902ab9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503554}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ee041a5d-3530-58d3-9ad7-acdf10ca4984" :question/math-academy-id "q-166761" :question/problem "Mary wonders where and when they'd meet if Sam left home $3.8$ minutes earlier and walked with a speed of $50$ meters per minute. She finds that the distance $d$ from home they'd meet can be modeled using the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}d+60t=960 \\\\ d-50t=190.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time (in minutes) since Mary left the community park.\n\nMary and Sam would meet$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$minutes after Mary left the community park.\n\nMary and Sam would meet at a distance of $\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,$meters from home." :question/worked-solution "To solve the given system of linear equations, we will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It doesn't matter which equation we pick first, so we choose the easiest one. In this case, the second equation looks like the easiest.\n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $d$ adding to both sides of the equation $50t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d-50t=190 \\\\ d=190+50t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $d$ with $190+50t$ in the first equation and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d+60t=960 \\\\ (190+50t)+60t & =960 \\\\ 190+110t & =960 \\\\ 110t & =960-190 \\\\ 110t & =770 \\\\ t & =\\frac{770}{110} \\\\ t & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, they would have met after $t=7$ minutes.\n\nIf we substitute $t=7$ into $d=190+50t$, we can find the value of $d:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =190+50t \\\\  & =190+50(7) \\\\  & =540\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, they meet at a distance of $540$ meters from home."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508171 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d8c7e85-9744-56b8-ad17-eac57676bf8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508177} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad2f379-b802-5a78-8607-922e2d09a5cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508211} {:answer/id #uuid "8c480585-9da5-5f00-8620-6f9f4b8471e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508212} {:answer/id #uuid "eda2dc78-3b71-5603-99bc-d2a18246622d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508237} {:answer/id #uuid "f85f3e50-67d1-5429-9721-b01c743f8a4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f85f3e50-67d1-5429-9721-b01c743f8a4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508239} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f3454ce-d4fe-5e69-9c29-1cf7c10c083c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508208}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "01d4210c-99cb-5509-8003-8615f9f2d644" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{3a-3b=-18; -2a+b=7$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2a+b & =7 \\\\ b & =7+2a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=7+2a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-3b & =-18 \\\\ 3a-3(7+2a) & =-18 \\\\ 3a-21-6a & =-18 \\\\ -3a-21 & =-18 \\\\ -3a & =3 \\\\ a & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-1$ into $b=7+2a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =7+2(-1) \\\\ b & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=-1-(5)=-6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508174 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d173c13-b0d2-5277-871e-ecb5b39a99ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d173c13-b0d2-5277-871e-ecb5b39a99ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508176} :answer-field/id #uuid "4806076d-709c-5c2f-9105-4634d0972c75" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508191} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cea1815-2688-56a2-b4ab-965679af5b0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cea1815-2688-56a2-b4ab-965679af5b0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508175} :answer-field/id #uuid "aeabe89b-5ecb-5574-b4fc-226f206baafd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508225}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1814dd75-6dc3-5a88-93bf-56fa1a5ec858" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{x+5y=21; y=x-3$\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.The solution is\n$($\n{{field-1}}\n$, $\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the second equation is already solved for $y:$\n\n$$\ny=x-3\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $y$ in the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5y & =21 \\\\ x+5(x-3) & =21 \\\\ x+5x-15 & =21 \\\\ 6x-15 & =21 \\\\ 6x & =36 \\\\ x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=6$ into $y=x-3,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(6)-3 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=6,\\,y=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508179 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70c5addc-2f92-5b2d-9cb9-315d42c2eaf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508203} {:answer/id #uuid "9c57a785-864f-578d-a998-d06a760a82b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508219} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc1215d-6449-5646-8c6a-c29cc1fa3226" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508220} {:answer/id #uuid "a49ee6a6-f0da-5faa-b3bf-a70649b568f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508223} {:answer/id #uuid "ea6e4596-9bcf-59c6-a3cb-0242f006b8e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a49ee6a6-f0da-5faa-b3bf-a70649b568f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508223} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6ff3c1c-579d-56f9-8656-874b7f2727c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508232}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e8faafd-e3ef-5205-a5d6-b458af26d97f" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{-3a-2b=2; -3a+b=8$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a+b & =8 \\\\ b & =8+3a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=8+3a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a-2b & =2 \\\\ -3a-2(8+3a) & =2 \\\\ -3a-16-6a & =2 \\\\ -9a-16 & =2 \\\\ -9a & =18 \\\\ a & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-2$ into $b=8+3a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =8+3(-2) \\\\ b & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=-2-(2)=-4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508187 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3eb5050b-2f97-532e-b6c8-5866bcc9fa51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3eb5050b-2f97-532e-b6c8-5866bcc9fa51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508188} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac08740b-e844-58dd-baf4-40ef0b885178" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f39f41a-cfb3-5bf0-b58f-8d17841342c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f39f41a-cfb3-5bf0-b58f-8d17841342c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508189} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa771fca-d97d-5b82-add7-3f2815e11284" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508240}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3db3cd07-1246-5ea5-a44f-5fee48dd9a13" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$\\{3x+3y=2; 3x+y=-5$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+y & =-5 \\\\ y & =-5-3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=-5-3x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+3y & =2 \\\\ 3x+3(-5-3x) & =2 \\\\ 3x-15-9x & =2 \\\\ -6x-15 & =2 \\\\ -6x & =17 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{17}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=-\\frac{17}{6}$ into $y=-5-3x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5-3(-\\frac{17}{6}) \\\\ y & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-\\frac{17}{6},\\,y=\\frac{7}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508204 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61123492-b1fa-52ea-a78d-92d15eb4799a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61123492-b1fa-52ea-a78d-92d15eb4799a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508201} :answer-field/id #uuid "00e813eb-39d3-591a-bc56-b776bdfd2316" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508170} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fc36be2-1ad6-5b03-b736-d29211c26e29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fc36be2-1ad6-5b03-b736-d29211c26e29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508194} :answer-field/id #uuid "84b6ed04-ec34-5023-a363-127985a3747a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508209}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "76c476e0-406c-5751-a806-f5cbe03fe610" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$\\{-3x+4y=8; -2x+y=6$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+y & =6 \\\\ y & =6+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=6+2x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+4y & =8 \\\\ -3x+4(6+2x) & =8 \\\\ -3x+24+8x & =8 \\\\ 5x+24 & =8 \\\\ 5x & =-16 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{16}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=-\\frac{16}{5}$ into $y=6+2x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =6+2(-\\frac{16}{5}) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-\\frac{16}{5},\\,y=-\\frac{2}{5}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508205 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b524116-52f0-5f16-ae76-c059374938ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508185} {:answer/id #uuid "7be0167d-61f1-500e-a6e6-d5a8f953e8c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508206} {:answer/id #uuid "904ce195-1201-5ff2-98fd-a1b9b5f6be03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508213} {:answer/id #uuid "979f6cea-60ca-5f62-beef-5756f8383e4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508217} {:answer/id #uuid "cfb36f0e-5371-55ee-b6e5-d11c77737dc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b524116-52f0-5f16-ae76-c059374938ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508185} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a85b03b-c3ea-57e4-a844-98bb80d07f7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508193}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7afeeb08-8b8f-54f1-86b4-033f592e20d8" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{-5a+2b=9; -3a+b=3$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a+b & =3 \\\\ b & =3+3a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=3+3a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5a+2b & =9 \\\\ -5a+2(3+3a) & =9 \\\\ -5a+6+6a & =9 \\\\ a+6 & =9 \\\\ a & =3 \\\\ a & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=3$ into $b=3+3a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =3+3(3) \\\\ b & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=3-(12)=-9.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508207 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32fad7a2-8a24-54a3-82c3-95bdccedab06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508183} {:answer/id #uuid "55557865-d7a4-5c61-a72d-2df58ccc52f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508196} {:answer/id #uuid "568a98b9-849b-5575-92e8-a07c6266f271" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508197} {:answer/id #uuid "afc824e1-f2ad-5146-9402-020f186abb13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508226} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4128bc-2e10-521b-aec7-327b7f86a452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afc824e1-f2ad-5146-9402-020f186abb13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508226} :answer-field/id #uuid "2074e8b8-4078-53a4-973e-82b464298bff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508178}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7c5faa09-66e6-54c1-b548-04286527c92b" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $p - q$?\n\n$\\{4p=-24; p+5q=19$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $p$ by dividing both sides by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4p & =-24 \\\\ p & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $p=-6$ into the second equation and solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p+5q & =19 \\\\ (-6)+5q & =19 \\\\ 5q & =25 \\\\ q & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p-q=-6-(5)=-11.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508210 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0095545e-54d6-52cd-924a-d0a5a2f5a1ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508169} {:answer/id #uuid "2f4bd4b3-9bdd-5c11-8b51-838c43d39c9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508180} {:answer/id #uuid "337996a5-122c-53fe-a44a-810d11d9fbdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508184} {:answer/id #uuid "3c4b4903-fe0a-5fb0-a751-3f0fa8df877f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508186} {:answer/id #uuid "6432dee2-0978-5e2c-8294-660f6ce4dc02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6432dee2-0978-5e2c-8294-660f6ce4dc02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508202} :answer-field/id #uuid "d61ec2e2-631a-51c9-9a12-395b3a9c74bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508231}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "873b7f6f-85bd-5d73-adb8-dc5d593e552e" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{-3a-3b=6; -4a+b=-7$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4a+b & =-7 \\\\ b & =-7+4a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=-7+4a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a-3b & =6 \\\\ -3a-3(-7+4a) & =6 \\\\ -3a+21-12a & =6 \\\\ -15a+21 & =6 \\\\ -15a & =-15 \\\\ a & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=1$ into $b=-7+4a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =-7+4(1) \\\\ b & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=1-(-3)=4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508214 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f716510c-61a9-5383-bd22-3d0176b54c16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "201" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f716510c-61a9-5383-bd22-3d0176b54c16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "201" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508238} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f59436d-c718-5b08-a237-9487d4690290" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508181} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "583c3fbc-a7f5-5eaf-9bde-02befa16b80a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "583c3fbc-a7f5-5eaf-9bde-02befa16b80a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508198} :answer-field/id #uuid "967e7c7f-52cd-501b-b2ff-8c12483f5017" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508216}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "92720f95-de85-556b-8f87-1b3810fd832e" :question/problem "The coefficients $a$ and $b$ satisfy $b=135-11a.$\n\nThe coefficients $a$ and $b$ also satisfy the equation $7b+162a=435.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$b\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}b=135-11a \\\\ 7b+162a=435\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the first equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=135-11a\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $b$ in the second equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7b+162a & =435 \\\\ 7(135-11a)+162a & =435 \\\\ 945-77a+162a & =435 \\\\ 945+85a & =435 \\\\ 85a & =-510 \\\\ a & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-6$ into $b=135-11a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =135-11(-6) \\\\ b & =201\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-6,\\,b=201.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508215 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a525fbe-b100-56e5-b363-b84bd9a5d52e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508173} {:answer/id #uuid "5b7578d1-6cb2-5958-9c79-b1f69ff339d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508199} {:answer/id #uuid "9fbaa74b-19ed-5c95-b977-ac0cc7054256" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508222} {:answer/id #uuid "b7b07809-444e-59d8-a95b-553b710baa60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508229} {:answer/id #uuid "eac62da3-8a0e-571b-9e13-3d68ba632045" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a525fbe-b100-56e5-b363-b84bd9a5d52e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508173} :answer-field/id #uuid "97f66384-4244-5039-a3bb-781c22ba011e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508218}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9362a51f-6c19-5264-931e-57aaf13ce3e6" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{-2a-4b=-14; -2a+b=6$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2a+b & =6 \\\\ b & =6+2a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=6+2a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2a-4b & =-14 \\\\ -2a-4(6+2a) & =-14 \\\\ -2a-24-8a & =-14 \\\\ -10a-24 & =-14 \\\\ -10a & =10 \\\\ a & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-1$ into $b=6+2a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =6+2(-1) \\\\ b & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=-1-(4)=-5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508227 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e04510d-2fe1-543a-ac55-911f068010c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e04510d-2fe1-543a-ac55-911f068010c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508221} :answer-field/id #uuid "496722ff-acc0-5b76-a13e-09917012d73d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508192} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08a38b64-b8c2-526f-8347-6ba7980eb350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08a38b64-b8c2-526f-8347-6ba7980eb350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508172} :answer-field/id #uuid "b547fc55-eab5-5d24-ba49-2faa2df55e6a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508228}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b0966484-f411-5cf8-8677-c24b7843a43c" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$\\{5x-2y=5; 2x+y=-1$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y & =-1 \\\\ y & =-1-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=-1-2x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-2y & =5 \\\\ 5x-2(-1-2x) & =5 \\\\ 5x+2+4x & =5 \\\\ 9x+2 & =5 \\\\ 9x & =3 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ into $y=-1-2x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1-2(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=\\frac{1}{3},\\,y=-\\frac{5}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508233 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "609dae4d-f20b-597d-8d5c-bd3985bfb3ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "609dae4d-f20b-597d-8d5c-bd3985bfb3ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508200} :answer-field/id #uuid "313ebe14-9bc4-580a-8ef0-cc446d43568b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508182} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54ede735-9e0a-5b8d-8cb8-1ec5b24e8a75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54ede735-9e0a-5b8d-8cb8-1ec5b24e8a75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508195} :answer-field/id #uuid "40fbd52d-5989-56ab-8589-60d240620d11" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508190}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ddedcc45-5aba-5229-89b3-d8e7abbe4344" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$\\{2x+2y=12; -2x+y=5$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+y & =5 \\\\ y & =5+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=5+2x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+2y & =12 \\\\ 2x+2(5+2x) & =12 \\\\ 2x+10+4x & =12 \\\\ 6x+10 & =12 \\\\ 6x & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ into $y=5+2x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5+2(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ y & =\\frac{17}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=\\frac{1}{3},\\,y=\\frac{17}{3}.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096649 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096446 :question/id #uuid "d1329498-4413-5d87-a814-be0d57a3afd0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4280" :question/problem "The vector $\\mathbf a$ is shown in the diagram below. Draw the vectors $2\\mathbf a$ and $-3\\mathbf a$.\n\n![](images/a5/a5eaa8baaf303ecbfa6c0fb207d6b19836cc90fc331e238cd473109f44fddf80.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $2\\mathbf{a}$ and $-3\\mathbf{a}$ must be parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nNow, for the vector $2\\mathbf{a}$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $2\\mathbf{a}$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n- Vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $2\\mathbf{a}$ have the same direction since the factor $2$ is positive.\n\n![](images/41/41eba7e6c5bbe420418726bd45efa668dc6be5ff5144ba35d52b53a43925c333.png)\n\nNext, for the vector $-3\\mathbf{a}$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $3\\mathbf{a}$ is $3$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n- Vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $-3\\mathbf{a}$ have opposite directions since the factor $-3$ is negative.\n\n![](images/ed/eda3f2572d98ef1789292ec6d35569487b32efa459673dcb95f8fdd0d1f4ae5b.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc49f831-8e1d-5fb4-8952-1dd4ee3bfa02" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049603 :topic/math-academy-id 1100 :topic/title "The Triangle Law for the Addition of Two Vectors"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096968 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84bcbe16-7536-5125-b103-ef9c458c9db5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d6/d6c501b98e6eb5b998b6ebf822ec33e23dc1e67c01e3424e571ac19ded016a9a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093783} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d252a8-1a3a-531e-aba7-030ccb0e8aaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fa/fafda2acdd5a0f4355abcb067afff9367a5cf10acbe0b22f976e165927c18968.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093784} {:answer/id #uuid "35f79dfb-e1f1-5ee4-86af-f6afc25792cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a1/a173c48fb3f47049dbf06ccaf4628313b367bdc0b7b2c18bd7a88a7ed33a2069.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093785} {:answer/id #uuid "38cf6707-6d85-5651-82d6-d2a22b325ed9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0b/0b48a668105d698a5c055839f09d7a10c9b5b8da63bc05ca5a948bb6eb3df730.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093786} {:answer/id #uuid "748ec053-3c16-52b1-aa52-badc0e6e736e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d2/d230aec47e23f7e1c8b03eeb2487b2c59d83e33bb1901b55070dd5647777dfd7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093787}] :answer-field/id #uuid "282b29ca-f425-5dfd-bd27-5209be89cfc7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answe